WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.970
[NARRATOR]
Far away, but not long ago,
Zoro found himself trapped

3
00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.960
<b>Ruins of the Muggy Kingdom
Gloom Island</b>

4
00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:53.480
on a certain gloomy island with Perona.

5
00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.630
The heck is this?

6
00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.290
It looks like a grave.

7
00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.630
The question's who made it?

8
00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.770
[ZORO]
Whoever they are,
they've got some skill.

9
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.900
It was carved straight
out of that tree.

10
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.040
[PERONA]
I dunno if this is
"good creepy" or "bad creepy."

11
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.580
[ZORO growls]

12
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:19.850
[ZORO gasps]

13
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.420
They're fast.

14
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.710
Damn it. He's strong, too!

15
00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.940
Uh-oh! Look out!

16
00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.080
[ZORO grunts]

17
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.820
[PERONA gasping]

18
00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.780
What are those things?

19
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.480
<b>The Land of Poverty, Hungeria
Lazy Bones Island</b>

20
00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.130
[NARRATOR]
This is Lazy Bones Island in
the Land of Poverty, Hungeria.

21
00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.330
Sent here by Kuma,

22
00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.800
Brook was mistaken for Satan
by the island's inhabitants.

23
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:38.290
[yawns]
How lovely!
Another perfect day!

24
00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.440
[screams]

25
00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.010
[WORSHIPPER D]
It's the Longarm Tribe!

26
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.310
Oh, no.

27
00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:50.880
[WORSHIPPER E groans]

28
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.540
[WORSHIPPER F gags]

29
00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.880
[GIRL A]
No! Help me!

30
00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.120
[SATAN WORSHIPPER G screams]

31
00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.290
[BROOK gasps]

32
00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.960
You're in trouble this
time! You hear me?

33
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.030
[WORSHIPPER I]
Put her down now!

34
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.170
[WORSHIPPER J]
We're not gonna warn you again!

35
00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.030
Let my daughter go!

36
00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:11.210
We've had enough of this!
We'll give you a taste of hell!

37
00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:16.080
[BROOK gasping]

38
00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:20.660
[screams]
Don't let them take me away!

39
00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.390
Uh, they're really kidnapping
her, aren't they?

40
00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:24.590
[WORSHIPPER L]
Uh-huh.

41
00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.400
[PEKKORI]
Unless you curse them!

42
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.900
Yes, now is the time!

43
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.630
[WORSHIPPERS]
Mm-hm. Mm-hm.

44
00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.100
[BROOK]
Never mind that!
Shouldn't we be chasing them?

45
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.400
[GIRL A]
Lord Satan!

46
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.700
[BROOK]
Uh?!

47
00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.870
We're too late.

48
00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.020
Did you hear us, Satan?

49
00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.060
[BROOK]
Huh?

50
00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.390
[PEKKORI]
Did you? We were cheering extra hard!

51
00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:46.660
You can save us now, oh Dark Lord!

52
00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.100
[WORSHIPPERS]
– Give it your best!
– Give it your best!

53
00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.200
[BROOK]
Oh... I see what got
them in this situation now.

54
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.900
They're lazy!

55
00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:59.270
[BROOK]
But that young lady is still a victim.

56
00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.310
I can't allow her to
suffer such a cruel fate.

57
00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.110
I will save her. At the very least,

58
00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.210
I owe for you the food.
Not to mention the panties.

59
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.250
[WORSHIPPERS cheer]

60
00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:18.220
[WORSHIPPERS]
– Lord Satan! Lord Satan!
– Lord Satan! Lord Satan!

61
00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:21.690
Lord Satan! Lord Satan!

62
00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:25.660
[BROOK]
You must forgive me, Luffy. Everyone.

63
00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:30.130
Right now I'm rather busy being
Satan in a sea of underwear.

64
00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.840
I'm afraid our reunion
will have to wait.

65
00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.240
I owe my odd new friends
a debt of gratitude.

66
00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.110
But I am confident that I
shall resolve this quickly,

67
00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.490
and I hope you keep safe until then.

68
00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:53.640
[NARRATOR]
Deep in the South
Blue lies Birdie Kingdom,

69
00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:57.110
<b>Birdie Kingdom
South Blue</b>

70
00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.360
where a race of giant
birds reign supreme.

71
00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:13.290
[sighs]
Oh, man, I really
want off this stinking island.

72
00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.500
This place is seriously the worst.

73
00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.340
[CHOPPER]
Birds treating me like I'm their toy.

74
00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:23.930
And humans constantly trying
to eat me in a hot pot.

75
00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:29.600
[CHOPPER]
If that's not
bad enough, and it really is,

76
00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.110
the birds and the humans won't
stop fighting each other.

77
00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:41.870
There's gotta be a way out of here.

78
00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.780
[chirps]

79
00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.440
[NARRATOR]
positioned deep in the Grand Line,

80
00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:59.870
we find Peachy Island, home
of the Kamabakka Kingdom.

81
00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:59.440
<b>Kamabakka Queendom
Peachy Island, Grand Line</b>

82
00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.970
[SANJI pants]
Where am I?

83
00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.700
I wasn't even looking.

84
00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.910
Am I safe in here?

85
00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:10.670
What the hell is wrong
with you psychos?!

86
00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:11.740
[laughs]

87
00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.810
[SANJI screams]

88
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:26.820
[groaning]
Ow.

89
00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.730
[CAROLINE]
I've been waitin' for you.

90
00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.890
[SANJI]
Uh...

91
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.670
You do not disrespect
her like that.

92
00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:42.410
Hey, hold on. Who is this bastard?

93
00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:58.610
[SANJI]
"Dear Nami and Robin, How are you?
I hope this finds you well.

94
00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.810
I do so look forward to
seeing the two of you again.

95
00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:07.080
I'm certain when that time comes,
we'll be better friends than ever before!"

96
00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:28.120
[NARRATOR]
Far away, but not long ago,
on a Sky Island known as Weatheria.

97
00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:34.010
A weather wizard, or rather a weather
scientist, continued his studies.

98
00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.940
<b>Weatheria</b>

99
00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.220
[HAREDAS]
Young lady!

100
00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.690
[NAMI gasps]

101
00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.960
Over here!

102
00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.520
[NAMI]
A ship?

103
00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.840
[NAMI]
Whoa. What the heck? It flies?

104
00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.590
[yelps]
Uh, no! No!

105
00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.860
Here we go!

106
00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.090
[NAMI]
Huh? [screams]

107
00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:16.340
That's the island I was
looking for, let's land there!

108
00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.360
[NAMI]
It's so dry.

109
00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:29.660
[MAYOR]
You can save our island?
And we're to believe that?

110
00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:30.860
[HAREDAS]
Why not?

111
00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:33.370
Thankfully, I'm an
expert with the weather.

112
00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.500
I'll gladly summon a shower or two!

113
00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:39.340
- [VILLAGERS gasp]
- [MAYOR] You jest!

114
00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:42.060
So, how about we make a little deal?

115
00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.760
Does a hundred million
berries sound fair?

116
00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:45.560
That's a lot!

117
00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.840
- [VILLAGERS gasp]
- [MAYOR sighs]

118
00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:51.810
[HAREDAS]
Hm? Did I highball it a bit?

119
00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:55.380
Are you kidding me?!
Do they look rich to you?!

120
00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:01.030
I see. Well, how does a hundred sound?

121
00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.800
- [NAMI] Huh?
- [VILLAGERS] So cheap!

122
00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:16.820
What's that? Soap bubbles, maybe?

123
00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:18.920
Looks like there's something inside.

124
00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:21.690
[HAREDAS laughs]
One more thing.

125
00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:25.230
Could you take this and generate
some wind for me, please?

126
00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:31.170
Oh, I see... Do you want it full power?

127
00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.830
[HAREDAS]
But of course!

128
00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.190
[villagers gasp]

129
00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:04.280
Rain clouds? But that can't be!

130
00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.170
[villagers cheer]

131
00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.630
[VILLAGER B]
It's raining!

132
00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.510
[VILLAGER C]
Yeah!

133
00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.510
[children laugh]

134
00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.850
[HAREDAS]
What did I tell you?

135
00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:44.900
[laughs]

136
00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.020
They sure are happy, aren't they?

137
00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:51.620
[HAREDAS]
The science of weather
has many wonderful applications!

138
00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.070
[NARRATOR]
This is the Mechanical Island,

139
00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.770
Future Land Baldimore,

140
00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:08.040
also known as the
birthplace of the Genius.

141
00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:09.250
<b>Mech Island
Futureland Baldimore</b>

142
00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.990
We better get him
to the hospital, Kitton.

143
00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:16.140
[KITTON]
Yeah.

144
00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.170
<b>Surgery in
Progress</b>

145
00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.250
[SURGEON 418A]
Well, he's definitely a cyborg.

146
00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.850
[SURGEON 418B]
I can't believe he runs on cola.

147
00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:45.020
[SURGEON 418C]
What should we do?

148
00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.250
We don't have any sodas to refuel him.

149
00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.820
[SURGEON 418B]
There's no time to lose.

150
00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:50.920
We need to begin.

151
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:51.920
[SURGEON 418A]
Right.

152
00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.090
<b>Surgery in
Progress</b>

153
00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.090
Hey, mister!

154
00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:20.960
Hello. You're the young
lad from earlier, correct?

155
00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:24.060
I do hope that I haven't
kept you waiting for too long.

156
00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.300
Yeah, you're definitely different.

157
00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.070
What did they do to you?

158
00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:32.000
[FRANKY]
Well it seems that
cola is hard to come by here,

159
00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.040
so they brewed up
some fine hot tea instead.

160
00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.100
Darjeeling, to be precise.

161
00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.570
Hot tea?

162
00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.400
The aroma and flavor are truly super.

163
00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:54.590
Lovely. There's really
nothing quite so relaxing.

164
00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:58.030
Okay. If you say so.

165
00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.090
I'm sorry, where are my manners?

166
00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.500
[FRANKY]
Enjoy. Careful, it's hot.

167
00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.540
No, no, this is weird! It's all wrong!

168
00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.400
Hey, Mister! You're not funny now.

169
00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.240
I liked you more the way you were!

170
00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:22.310
Oh? Is that so?

171
00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.820
[FRANKY]
It's cold!

172
00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.560
How on earth I did I end up
out here in the elements?

173
00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:58.600
Ah! How lovely, a scarf for me? Thanks.

174
00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.970
[FRANKY]
Oh my, oh my, oh my, oh my!

175
00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:08.700
Goodness!

176
00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.700
This... This is the nightmare!

177
00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:20.210
[FRANKY]
"Keep Out, this is an enclosed
forest of mechanical animals."

178
00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.020
[CYBORG ANIMALS clamor]

179
00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:37.030
[cyborg animals growl]

180
00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.150
Ready for plan A: Surprise
Awakening in the Jungle!

181
00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:54.820
[Taromino pants]

182
00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.020
[KITTON]
Nothing's more wild than mecha animals!

183
00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.420
This'll get him back on
track for sure! [laughs]

184
00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.630
Now, now, let's all calm
down, shall we be friends?

185
00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:04.760
Because you seem agitated this morning.

186
00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:06.840
Did you remember to eat your breakfast?

187
00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.140
It is the most important
meal of the day, you know.

188
00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.600
Let's work on getting those
blood sugar levels up!

189
00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:12.890
[cyborg animals growl]

190
00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:17.310
Huh? Hold on a second, that means
it's breakfast time for me, too!

191
00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:21.610
Ahhh, you silly goose! Ha, ha, ha.

192
00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:29.790
Delicious! No better way to start
the day than with a cup of tea! Ha!

193
00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.320
Would you care for
some tea, too?

194
00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.500
Ah! Let's cherish
every moment, friends!

195
00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.140
[KITTON]
Ah... It's not working!

196
00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.260
[Kitton, Taromino gasp]

197
00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:52.390
- [cyborg ape whoops]
- [Kitton screams]

198
00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.020
[Kitton screaming]

199
00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:13.320
Someone help us!

200
00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.450
Violence is never the a...!

201
00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.740
[Franky groans]

202
00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:24.540
I know that you're at an age
when you want to be naughty.

203
00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:29.920
But listen... we can...
sort this out...

204
00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:32.290
like gentlemen, right?

205
00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:37.050
Nothing... good... ever
comes... from violence!

206
00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.760
Come on, just fight back! Please!

207
00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.050
You can't reason with gorillas!

208
00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:43.760
Rela...

209
00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.160
Listen to... Listen to what
I to what I have to...

210
00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:51.730
If you'd let me talk... I
have... wisdom to impart!

211
00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:54.360
To...

212
00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:59.230
My friend... we must... not...

213
00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.230
We...

214
00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:21.740
[FRANKY]
Ohh, yeah! Super!

215
00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:26.480
[FRANKY yells]

216
00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.880
Who do you think I am,
you punks, chopped liver?

217
00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:33.720
You can't step to Franky!

218
00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:37.120
He's back! You were seriously
starting to scare me!

219
00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:40.660
[FRANKY]
Oh yeah, wow!

220
00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.230
[KITTON]
What's wrong?

221
00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:48.030
[FRANKY]
I cooled off a bit and
ran out of steam, literally.

222
00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:51.520
Huh? You mean... you're
gonna turn back?

223
00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:55.120
Oh, I know just
the place to go!

224
00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.370
My Grandpa told me there's
some dangerous stuff in there.

225
00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.020
But it's an emergency and I have you
to protect me, so it should be okay.

226
00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:15.200
[thud]

227
00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:29.450
<b>Tequila Wolf
East Blue</b>

228
00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.320
Here's your breakfast,
lunch, and dinner.

229
00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.520
Once you finish that, we'll
get back to our questioning.

230
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.290
Oh, I can hardly wait.

231
00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.490
[CAPTAIN JERK chuckles]

232
00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:40.760
[ROBIN gasps]

233
00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:47.900
[MAN A]
Not to intrude, but it sounds like
you've been hurt pretty bad, young lady.

234
00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:48.970
Who...

235
00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:50.940
[MAN A]
Just a decrepit old man.

236
00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:53.640
I've only been in this
country for a single day now,

237
00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:56.340
but the guards in charge said
the elderly are useless,

238
00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.380
so they promptly threw me in here.

239
00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.930
I'm so sorry to hear that.
But I know how you feel.

240
00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.500
- [explosion]
- What the...?

241
00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:04.500
[SORAN]
Ah!

242
00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.630
[ARMY AGENT A]
There's a band
of dissidents running wild!

243
00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:13.200
The warden called for backup!

244
00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.830
He ordered all of us to get over there!

245
00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:15.710
[SLAVERS]
– Sir!
– Sir!

246
00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.640
A band of dissidents?

247
00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:22.610
[CAPTAIN JERK]
Yes, sir.

248
00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.610
But we were quick to
follow your orders, sir.

249
00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.350
All teams descended on the group,
so it didn't get out of hand.

250
00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:32.790
[SLAVER CAPTAIN]
What're you talking about,
I didn't give any orders!

251
00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.520
Don't tell me when you say "all teams",

252
00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:38.230
do you mean the soldiers
stationed at the prison tower?

253
00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:39.490
[SORAN]
Hey!

254
00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:46.510
I'm an agent working for
the revolutionary army.

255
00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:48.660
You fool!

256
00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.030
You really think I give a
damn about the dissidents?

257
00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:52.900
Take down Nico Robin
on sight, men!

258
00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:56.700
Then good work.

259
00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.300
[ARMY AGENT A]
With your command of our
forces, I know we can win.

260
00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:01.980
[MAN A]
Well. You can count on me.

261
00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:03.970
Oh, before we go. Release
the young lady from her cell.

262
00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:05.930
She's already been
through enough as it is.

263
00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.690
Nico Robin! Kill her!

264
00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:21.070
And Clutch!

265
00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:29.080
[slavers groaning]

266
00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.120
[men gasp]

267
00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.080
The Nico Robin?

268
00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.390
<b>Bowin Archipelago
Grand Line</b>

269
00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:46.940
[USOPP sighs]
Whoa! What the hell is this place?

270
00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.300
It smells so good!

271
00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:53.800
Who would eat bugs when
you got stuff like this?!

272
00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:57.340
[HERACLES]
Ramen Falls'n! Spaghetti Patches'n!

273
00:21:57.340 --> 00:21:59.510
Ham Fruits'n!

274
00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:02.240
Chocolate Rocks'n.

275
00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:04.840
Take whatever you want.
It's all safe to eat.

276
00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:08.710
So I'm okay to eat this too, right?

277
00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.950
[HERACLES]
Right. Eat your fill!

278
00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:16.200
Once you've had enough to
build up your stamina,

279
00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:19.070
the man-eating plants'n
won't mess with you!

280
00:22:19.070 --> 00:22:20.490
[USOPP]
Sure, right, good plan.

281
00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:23.660
This stuff is so good I feel
like I could eat forever!

282
00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:25.370
[HERACLES]
Eating's only the first step!

283
00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:27.250
You've gotta exercise, too!

284
00:22:27.250 --> 00:22:28.710
[USOPP]
Well, yeah, obviously!

285
00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:30.420
But I'm still on the first step here!

286
00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:34.450
I've gotta bulk up so I can become a cool
hero of the forest like you, right?

287
00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:44.580
Oh, man, I can't eat another bite!

288
00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:46.020
[HERACLES]
Usopp'n.

289
00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:49.950
Don't you realize fat things are the first
creatures to be eaten on this island?

290
00:22:49.950 --> 00:22:52.020
Wait, are you talking about me?

291
00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:55.690
[HERACLES]
It's impossible to
escape from the Bowin Islands!

292
00:22:55.690 --> 00:22:58.260
Why didn't you tell me that before?

293
00:22:58.260 --> 00:22:59.330
[HERACLES]
As for me.

294
00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:01.370
I'm the hero of the forest. Her...
